  "title": "Erdős Problem #404",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For which integers $a\\geq 1$ and primes $p$ is there a finite upper bound on those $k$ such that there are $a=a_1<\\cdots<a_n$ with $ p^k \\mid (a_1!+\\cdots+a_n!)? $ If $f(a,p)$ is the greatest such $k$, how does this function behave?\nIs there a prime $p$ and an infinite sequence $a_1<a_2<\\cdots$ such that if $p^{m_k}$ is the highest power of $p$ dividing $\\sum_{i\\leq k}a_i!$ then $m_k\\to \\infty$?",
